 "notes": "Per-monster hints for tools/body_gen/proc_motion.py (Tripo 'Other' auto-rig: generic bone names, patchy weights). Coordinates are armature space of the Tripo FBX (forward -Y, up +Z, the creature's left = +X, about 1 unit). cleanup: mesh_cleanup.py options run before rigging (new_vertex_bone: bone for the vertices it adds). fix: rig repairs - the mesh is never moved, only bones/weights: add_chain = new bone chain through points, the vertices it takes (only_dominant / only_dominant_match bones, inside box or more_boxes) re-weighted by projection onto the chain, blended into blend_parent at its base, refine = re-centre inner joints in the skin; mirror_chain = copy a leg chain to the other side with mirrored weights; split = new bone that takes the skin above (or below: true) a line in the (y,z) plane; delete = bones left without skin. legs: name -> {ik: hip..ankle bones, foot: bone held flat (null = the mesh tip of the last ik bone)}; the other keys name the bones each species' motion program drives. build_bones: copy into game_build.json 'bones' (Mixamo names the build measures -> this rig's bones).",
